## Done when

- [ ] `PoolGrid.tsx` changed as in Steps 3–7. No other source file changed.
- [ ] `PoolGrid.render.test.tsx`'s three tests pass, and so do the deck builder, almanac and `TermTip` tests.
- [ ] `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, typecheck and eslint run. Every red test is named in the report (see Risks).
- [ ] The PR has the baseline, before and after table, says why `SLOW_GRID` stays, and records the decisions below.
- [ ] The preview servers are stopped, `sh scripts/browse.sh close` has run, and `/tmp/jackioh-baseline` is gone.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass.

## Risks

- **Stale handlers.** A memoized card must never keep an old `onAdd`: DeckEditor's `add` closes over `deck.cards`. The `latest` ref makes the handlers stable without going stale, and test 2 guards it. Never drop the callbacks from `samePoolItem`.
- **The deferred list.** While a grown pool's background render runs, the grid briefly shows the cards it drew before, while the count already shows the new number. Under `act`, every unit test flushes the background render. Cypress queries retry (`33-almanac`, `09-deckbuilder` and `deckbuilder-layout.cy.tsx` wait with `should("have.length", …)`). Don't defer a shrinking pool: the planner measured a narrowing search at 87–94 ms that way, against 42–46 ms.
- **Contexts.** Locale, settings, picks and inspect state reach a card through its own hooks (`useLocale`, `useFullArt`, `useInspectTrigger`), so the memo does not freeze them. The R1956000 tests in `PoolGrid.test.tsx` and `almanac.test.tsx` check this.
- **A failure that is already on main.** `src/cards/textLimit.test.ts` "B15 R1017000 the premise…" fails on unchanged main 795c3f2 (traininggrounds-039 has no short form). The planner ran it on main and saw it fail. It is not this change. Name it in the report, and don't call it green.

## Open questions

The planner measured in headless Chromium at 1280x720 with the script above, two runs each, in ms:

| | baseline 9be40af (481 cards) | main (709) | this plan (709) |
|---|---|---|---|
| open: first cards / longest frame | 259–260 / 259 | 349–361 / 348–360 | 81–85 / 99–101 |
| open: whole grid in the DOM | 259–260 | 349–361 | 378–453 |
| search "dra": longest frame | 51–53 | 61–63 | 42–46 |
| clear search: first / longest frame | 271–279 | 338–349 | 69–74 / 90–92 |
| clear search: whole grid | 271–279 | 338–349 | 333–343 |
| open a detail | 74–87 | 109–111 | 25–26 |
| scroll: mean / p95 frame | 30–31 / 46 | 31 / 51 | 31 / 49–52 |

1. Building all 709 faces in the background, and the scroll p95, stay behind the 481-card baseline. The page still answers within about 100 ms. Matching those numbers too would need row virtualization or cheaper faces (the per-face IntersectionObservers and the fitting), which belongs in a follow-up issue. Does "every metric at or better" count these two?
2. Rejected: making each keyword a stateless element with one shared, delegated tooltip controller. Built and measured, it changed nothing (open 367–402 ms against main's 345–368 ms, and about 3% under jsdom). So R2098000's code stays as it is.
3. Rejected: removing `SLOW_GRID`, since the tests would sit at 3.6–4.5 s against a 5 s default.
